     How I Farmed My Way to the /dev/null Reanger High Score 

WARNING: Long, boring post containing graphic description of black 
pudding farming, not suitable for all readers. Contains slight 
duplications from the post mentioned in the next paragraph.

This was my sixth ascension, first Ranger ascension, and my second 
ascension in the /dev/null/net NetHack Tournament. Although this was my 
sixth ascension, this is my only my second ascension post. I usually 
start composing one, but tend to ramble on too much, and get distracted 
by something, and never finish it. However, see Message-ID: 
<nhplayer-A39CCA.11532604122004@comcast.dca.giganews.com> for my 
previous ascension post.

I started playing soon after midnight on the first day of the 
tournament, but had a real tough time getting a character to survive. I 
started playing tourists, since that had been my last ascension, but 
wasn't getting anywhere. So for the first ten days I played a succession 
of games as tourists, archeologists, rangers, rogues, archeologists, 
rangers, and rogues again. Finally, after about 35 games, I got a rogue 
that seemed to have some staying power. I played the rogue for several 
days and decided to start another game on another server. Rangers were 
the characters I had been playing on nethack.alt.org (nao, where I 
regularly play) and I always played Hum-Mal-Neu. But I wanted to qualify 
for some of the extra awards if I could manage to ascend the character, 
so I chose Elf-Mal-Cha. I should have picked Elf-Fem-Cha, but that's 
dealt with in the other post. So this is the tale of the ranger game 
started on 11/19. Note that the tournament is nearly two-thirds over 
already. 

I didn't save my starting stats, but here are the ones I saved as soon 
as I remembered:

Art the Lookout     St:15 Dx:15 Co:15 In:15 Wi:13 Ch:7  Chaotic S:464
Dlvl:2  $:4  HP:28(28) Pw:15(15) AC:6  Xp:3/47 T:1217


Again, I don't remember a lot about the early game and my notes never 
seem to contain the info I want. Anyway, according to my notes, I found 
a 6 x 9 general store on level 2. I spend a lot of time in the shops 
naming every item with it's base price, and then trying to get my pet to 
steal anything useful I can't afford to buy. I bought speed boots and 
and a lamp priced as magic. Punky, my dog, nicked a ?oEW, a ?oEAorRC, 
and several other scrolls and potions for me. It seemed like a promising 
beginning. The entrance to the mines were on level 4, and the first 
level was lit, but I skipped them. I got telepathy on level 5 and found 
a 2 x 5 general  store on level 6.  I bought 2 ?oID and a tin. There was 
also an altar to Mars(chaotic) on level 6.

The Oracle was on level 7 and, thus, the entrance to Sokoban on level 8. 
I usually do Sokoban before the mines, so I entered Sokoban. There is 
nothing in the notes about solving Sokoban, so I assume nothing of 
interest happened there. I got the amulet of reflection about turn 7753 
and wore it for quite a long time. I noted that there was a black 
unicorn waiting in the zoo and left. Back on level 8, I advanced my 
skills to expert in dagger and skilled in bow at turn 8402. I found a 4 
x 9 liquor store with several 300 zm. potions, but didn't buy or nick 
anything. I decided to head to Minetown.

There was an icebox on level 5M, but it didn't have any useful corpses 
in it so I left it there. I never did try to move it to a base camp. 
Elves' carrying capacity really sucks. I got to Minetown on level 8M 
without any noteworthy occurrences. The temple was lawful, but I made a 
contribution and only got 2 points of protection. The shops were 
unusally bad, as I recall, with nothing worth buying or stealing. 
Without magic or poison resistance, I was reluctant to venture any lower 
in the mines and, so, returned to the main dungeon. I got vault sounds 
on level 4 and found and looted the vault, but I'm not sure if I did 
that then or later.

On level 9, I found a bones level for todd, who appeared to be a wizard 
from the makeup of the bones pile: a quarterstaff, leather armor, a 
cloak, some potions (including 2 smokey potions), scrolls, rings, a wand 
and a magic marker. I took out todd's ghost and the hounds took care of 
a cat (probably todd's pet) before I could get to it and tame it. I 
found a chest near the entry stairs and used it for a stash. I moved the 
bones loot into the stash chest without realizing I probably had a cloak 
of magic resistance now. Then there was a Deli on the level, empty 
except for an icebox with some useless corpes and a couple of potions, 
one of them smokey. I price ided smokey potions at 50 zm. I later found 
a robe when I killed a wererat.  I also found a poly trap near the 
downstairs and rolled a boulder over it to prevent the hounds from 
falling victim before I had a magic whistle to help control the outcome. 
Almost as soon as I did it, I realized that I couldn't move it off until 
I had MR too. Oh well. I proceeded deeper. 

I heard vault sounds on level 12, got the plea for help from Orion on 
level 13, and found a 5 x 6 liquor store also on level 13. I bought 3 50 
zm. smokey potions (although I think the bastard shopkeeper charged me 
99 zm. for them). Since they were 50 zm. potions, the worst that could 
happen was a little confusion, so I headed back to the altar on level to 
b/u/c test all the smokey potions and bless them up for a crack at a 
wish.

I apparently saved the game at this point and resumed the rogue game 
mentioned earlier. I resumed the game on 11/24. I blessed the smokey 
potions and got a wish from one of them. Smokey potions turned out to be 
booze in this game, so I drank a whole lot. I made a minor blunder at 
this point in the game. Well, actually I made the blunder somewhat 
earlier, but suffered its consequences now. In one of the shops, I had 
found an expensive bag, but it didn't seem to help unburden me, so I had 
named it Oilskin. I was having serious weight capacity problems, so I 
pondered for a long time whether to wish for a bag of holding or for 
gray dragon scale mail for the magic resistance. Finally I remembered 
that cloak that probably was magic resistance, reasoned that GDSM would 
only reduce my AC a couple of more points (was wearing +0 dwarvish 
mithril), and decided to go for the bag of holding. I think that was one 
of the reasons I had saved the game: to weigh that decision. Imagine my 
shock when the wished for bag showed up in my inventory as a greased bag 
named Oilskin. Next, imagine my annoyance when I burned a precious ?oID 
on it and verified that it was a bag of holding, not an oilskin bag, and 
that I had had one all along and had basically just thrown away a GDSM. 
I went back to my stash on level 9 to ditch one of the BoH, before I 
blew them both up (I manage to do that with embarrassing frequency). On 
the way, I finally got poison resistance at turn 19110 on level 7, and 
cold resistance at turn 19261 on level 9. 

I stashed the other BoH in my trunk and verified that the cloak was MR. 
I don't remember if I had to uncurse it or not, but I was now ready to 
take on the lower mines. I had even more incentive now: I'm really 
hoping for the Gnome King's Wine Cellar and 6 more smokey potions. I 
stopped at the Altar on level 6 for a while on the way to the mines. I 
remembered to name an elven dagger Sting this time and I got 
Stormbringer as my first sacrificial gift. I'm reluctant to use it much 
while I'm still using pets, so I put it away for a while. Alas, I got 
the Mimic of the Mines version and found nothing noteworthy in the mines 
at all. Except the luckstone, of course. I finished Minesend at turn 
22322 and headed back to base camp, with a stopover in Minetown to b/u/c 
test my swag. Up to this point, I've only learned 4 spells: Knock, 
Restore Ability, Force Bolt, and Healing. I'm still wearing mithril so 
my failure rates are all 100%. I'm still only XP 11, so I can't 
undertake the quest yet. I explore downward. 

I managed to kill poor Blue, one of my large dogs, when he stepped 
between me and something I was chucking daggers at without me noticing 
it. I felt bad about that. Really. I noted a black unicorn on the level 
and continued downward. Level 15 had a small beehive, 2 x 5, and I got 4 
lumps of royal jelly. But I had already reached strength 18, the max for 
an elf, so it was no big deal. Level 16 had another lawful temple, but I 
didn't have enough gold for another contribution yet. Level 18 was the 
Rogue Level and level 19 had the portal to Fort Ludious, but I don't 
remember if I discovered that at this time or later. Probably later when 
I'm actively looting vaults. Fell through some levels at this point and 
wound on on level 23, where there was a 1 x 4 barracks. I found the 
downstairs first and looked down and saw a zoo, whose size I didn't 
record, on level 24. 

Climbing back up, I found a third lawful temple on level 22. This 
imbalance would eventually have to be rectified. Level 21 contained 
another barracks, 2 x 5 this time. I found Vorpal Blade just lying on 
the dungeon floor, also on level 21. I didn't plan to use it at all, but 
I was happy to find it since there have been several reports recently of 
players reaching the Astral Plane, only to be beheaded by one of the 
adventurers there wielding a highly enchanted Vorpal Blade. At least 
now, I didn't have to worry about that prospect. Evidently I collected 
enough gold for 2 more protection contributions to the temple on level 
22, once at turn 29299 and again at turn 31388. There was a 2 x 3 
cockatrice nest on level 19 and then I headed back to the stash on level 
9. I apparently identified some of the hard gems I had discovered during 
the game and managed to stalk down the black unicorn on level 14 twice 
and tossed it 2 IDed gems to max out my luck.

My next note is dated 11/25, but I think it was the same session. I 
probably started it in the evening and played on until early morning. I 
usually play at night, but often don't start until after midnight. I 
think I started this session earlier than usual because time was running 
out. I guess I made it to XP level 13 about this time and probably used 
a potion of gain level to get to XP 14 and qualify for the quest. That 
seems to be what usually happens. So I headed for the quest.

There's a pit at the beginning of the path into the woods that leads to 
Orion's camp on the first level of the Ranger quest. I had never found a 
magic whistle and couldn't get any of my pets to cross the pit and join 
me on the quest. Oh well. It would be lonely, but that meant I could use 
Stormbringer without worry. So what if I piss off an occasional peaceful 
centaur? Nothing noteworthy seemed to happen along the way to the quest. 
The centaurs and scorpions seemed to take a while to die to 
Stormbringer, I don't think I had been able to enchant it much by then, 
but they did eventually die. Usually without doing too much damage to 
me. It got a little tense when I confronted Scopius; he kept making me 
sick. My unihorn would cure it, but it didn't seem like I was making any 
headway. But finally he died. I guess Stormbringer's level drains 
eventually wore him down. I picked up the Longbow of Diana and the Bell 
of Opening at turn 34435. I finished off the rest of riff raff and 
scoured the level for booty, but didn't find anything that merited a 
mention in my notes. I tried Scopius' throne until it vanished but the 
only positive outcome was: "You feel much much better". 

I didn't have any means of teleport control, so I had to slog all the 
way back to Orion's camp on foot. I reported in and looted his treasure 
chest. I learned the sleep spell, but was so burdened I left the 
spellbook there. There was a pit in the first leg of the path leading 
out of Orion's camp and one of the hunters had wandered out there and 
wouldn't come back to let me pass. I stood at the entry way where two 
people can pass, waiting and trying to block other hunters from 
entering, not always successfully. I must of spent several hundred turns 
waiting to get out of there. But I eventually did. I was seriously 
considering unleashing Stormbringer on the a**hole, but wasn't sure what 
that would do to my karma. I can't remember if I had to retame any of 
the pets when I got out of the woods, or not, but headed back to base 
camp. I noted that I completed the quest at turn 37145 on 11/25.

I moved my base camp from level 9 to the temple on level 16. I was 
worried about attacking the priest with Stormbringer inadvertently, but 
managed to avoid it. I scrounged up a chest (or large box), dug a niche 
in one of the temple walls, burned Elbereth on the floor, and moved all 
my stash there. I proceeded to b/u/c test all the loot I brought back 
from the quest. The two spellbooks were uncursed, so I read them. The 
first was detect food: ho hum. But the second was identify. Hoo boy! Now 
I'm in business. And there was much rejoicing. I had learned detect 
monster earlier, so I kept casting that until I could #enhance 
divination spells. Then, without my mithril and wearing the robe I found 
earlier,  I could cast identify at 0% failure. Finally, about turn 
38500, I was able to identify all my possessions. I found a ring of 
teleport control in my ring collection

Resuming my explorations, I found Grimtooth at turn 40993 on 11/27. 
There's a gap in my notes here. According to the notes, I didn't play on 
11/26 (nor in my rogue game). But I'm pretty sure I was playing almost 
as much as possible since the tournament was rapidly coming to an end. I 
can only assume that some of the events labeled as 11/25 actually 
happened on 11/26 and I just got confused on the dates. I found and 
looted a couple of more vaults on levels 23 and 24 and used the proceeds 
for three more protection contributions to the priest on level 22, 
bringing my AC down to -20. I found the right hand castle version of 
Medusa's level on level 25 and then headed back to base camp. I gathered 
up enough gold for another contribution by the time I got back to level 
16.

I was beginning to get desperate. After a promising start, the flow of 
goodies had dried to a trickle. I was still missing several key items: 
ring of slow digestion, ring of free action, ring of conflict, ring  of 
levitation (I had levitation boots), scroll of genocide, gray or silver 
dragon scale mail (I think I had made some blue). I needed the Castle 
WoW to fill out my Ascension Kit. I decided to level 'port to the level 
below Medusa and come back up and take care of her, since I wasn't keen 
on facing the Titan in the entrance hall nor the ;'s in water. Level 26 
was an ordinary dungeon level. I found the down stairs before the 
upstairs to Meduas. Level 27 was the Castle level. I offed Medusa at 
turn 45702 without any problem, but now faced the same problem with the 
;'s in the Castle moat. I wasn't keen on the idea of a full frontal 
assault on the Castle nor trying to levitate along the moat and facing 
the ;'s. So I decided to level 'port to the Valley of the Dead, hoping 
to land near the upstairs, as I had always seemed to do in the past. I 
did and only had to fight one or two monsters before I could make it up 
the stairs. 

I had used a similar tactic in my rogue ascension, and fear I may be 
mixing up some of the details with that game. Anyhow, I went in the back 
door and levitated over to the dragon stalls. I wanted to check the 
store rooms for useful armor and weapons. I was also hoping for a gray 
or silver dragon, but didn't get either of those. There was nothing 
useful in the store rooms, so I continued on to the back door of the 
throne room. After opening the door, I backed up to the far side of the 
first trap door, and watched as most of the residents came rushing out 
and fell through to the VotD. I'd deal with them later, right now I 
wanted that wand. After most of them fell through, I moved into the 
throne room and cleaned up the stragglers. The throne vanished on the 
first sitting, IIRC. I picked up the available booty and found the wand 
at turn 46661 on 11/27. It was only (0:1). I level 'ported back to base 
camp on level 16.

I now have 5 wishes available, but there are quite a few things I want 
and/or need. More that 5, anyway. I already have a blessed scroll of 
charging, so I don't need to wish for that. I used my first wish for 3 
blessed scrolls of genocide and got rid of L's,
h's, and ;'s. The second went for a helm of brilliance, but I didn't 
note what enchantment I got. I was about to wish for some dragon scale 
mail, when I realized a cursed scroll of genocide might be a better 
solution. I used my third wish for a magic marker and saved the final 2 
for later. I wrote a cursed scroll of genocide and called in some gray 
dragons. I was in the Temple of Mercury that I was using for a base camp 
and kind of hoped that the Temple priest my succumb to collateral 
damage. I edged out the door to fight them one at a time. The first one 
left scales, so I read a scroll of taming and got a pet gray dragon I 
named Twinkie in honor of several cats named Twinkie who had become 
various kinds of dragons (and one mind flayer) who had helped me out in 
other games. Between us, Twinkie and I took out the other 3 gray 
dragons. Unfortunately, the priest survived. I ate one of the dragon 
corpses and Twinkie consumed the other two. So then I stepped outside 
the Temple until "I heard some noises." When I went back in, the priest 
had mysteriously vanished, so I converted the altar to Mars at turn 
47272.

I thought about what I still needed to finish the game. There was now a 
huge mob waiting for me in the VotD and also that annoying Titan on 
Medusa's level. I thought of a scheme for avoiding most of that hassle. 
If I could come up with 4 cursed potions of gain level, I could use one 
to escape the Sanctum, one for the VotD, one for the Castle, and one for 
Medusa's level. On the way down, I could level 'port into VotD and then 
level 'port right down to the next level. That meant losing all the 
treasures in the VotD, but it seemed like a reasonable trade-off. A good 
batch of potions as raw material should make 4 potions of gain level an 
easy goal for some alchemy. So I decided to set up a small scale farm 
and black pudding farm for a while for a supply of raw materials.

I didn't have the proper resources to set up a proper farm. I didn't 
have Magicbane to engrave Elbereth under each of the boulders of a fort 
nor enough charges of fire or lightning wands. So it wouldn't be long 
before some giants came along and busted up the fort. So giants had to 
go. I wrote blessed scroll of genocide and goodbye giants. Still had to 
worry about Titans, but they probably wouldn't be a problem for a while, 
since I'm still only XP level 15. I also didn't know the light spell 
yet, so I'd have to leave the level dark. I built a small fort using the 
Temple walls as back ups and dug out the center area of the level. Since 
this was to be a fairly short order farm (only 3 days left in the 
tournament) I didn't clear out the whole level and double wall my fort 
as I usually would. Twinkie patrolled the level for me while I cleared 
it. Then I put Twinkie out to pasture on Home level 1 at turn 50609 and 
went back and used a cursed scroll of genocide for my starter herd of 
black puddings. I made my first prayer after a pudding sacrifice at turn 
50801 and harvested my first item, a scroll of enchant armor, at turn 
50843, at which time I also got a gift of protection bringing my AC to 
-35. A hundred turns later, a golden glow brought my HP to 205. I 
continued for a few hundred more turns and got my score to 500,549 at 
turn 51137, saved the game and knocked off for the day.

The next day was devoted to finishing up my rogue game as described in 
the YATAP referenced near the beginning of this post. I started my next 
session of this game very early on 11/29. I continued killing a batch of 
puddings and sacrificing them, praying whenever possible. I was told 
that I needed to play the right tune to enter the castle and then given 
the tune, even though I had already been to the Castle and got the wand. 
I also got 20 more HP, 2 more points of AC, and a spellbook of extra 
healing. But this was going way too slow; I had less than 48 hours left. 
So I decided to mostly stop sacrificing and hoped that I could 
accumulate enough potions and scrolls (as well as other needed items) 
via death drops to get my HP and AC to acceptable levels. I played this 
game on the Minnesota server, which seemed to be quite a bit faster than 
the California server where I played the rogue game, which now proved to 
be a big help.

I went into overdrive killing black puddings and any other hapless 
monsters that wandered up to the alter. Score was 1,000,125 at turn 
53788. From that point on, I only checked the loot every 1 million 
points or when a scroll of scare monster was death dropped, stopping the 
assembly line. I didn't keep track of the ordinary death drop items, but 
I noted a magic whistle at turn 59378, a ring of free action and 2 
touchstones at turn 63966, wands of polymorph and enlightenment and a 
magic marker at turn 65969. The 70,000's were kind of fallow, but a 
magic lamp showed up at turn 79525. I decided to use any wishes that 
came along to try for the Master Key of Thievery for its half damage 
property, so I blessed up the lamp and tried, but no go. I also got a +6 
ring of increase damage in this harvest. I think that's the highest 
enchantment I've ever encountered on a random ring. Score is now up to 7 
million plus.

At some point it occurred to me that at this rate I can spend a couple 
of more hours and have a score comparable to the rogue score. The record 
score for a ranger up to this point is 13 million and change, so I 
decide to shoot for a couple of million more than that. That will give 
my a shot if I don't manage to ascend and will be doubled if I do 
ascend, for an even better shot. The flow of goodies slowed even more. 
That's partially because my Ascension Kit is filling out and so there 
are fewer items now that are noteworthy. At turn 97751 the score is 
12,000,161 and the harvest contains a ring of conflict, a pair of 
jumping boots, and another magic lamp. I used the lamp wish for the MKOT 
again and was again unsuccessful. The score reached 14,000,829 at turn 
105885 and I decided to shut down the farm. I switched to a silver saber 
and slaughtered the remaining puddings and all the other accumulated 
hostile monsters.

A ring of slow digestion was the main item still missing from my 
ascension kit. Of course, I would like to have had the MKOT and 
Magicbane, but time was running out. I had kept polyless conduct up to 
now, but I decided to break it to try for a ring of slow digestion and 
save my 2 remaining wishes for emergencies. Besides, I had accumulated 
several wands of poly and lots of ring fodder from farming. I made 
several piles of rings and started zapping and soon had my ring of slow 
digestion. 

I gathered all the potions I had and pored oven the alchemy spoilers 
looking for useful transmutations. I dipped a unihorn into all my 
potions of sickness to convert them to fruit juice, combined them with 
all the fruit juice I had and dipped them into a potion of speed to 
produce booze. Dipped the rest of the speed I had into a potion of fruit 
juice (saving a couple of potions of speed for the healing to extra 
healing change) to make even more booze. Booze was smokey, so I blessed 
them up and went on a bender. I had over 50 blessed potions of booze and 
was quaffing away when I noticed I was satiated. I don't think I had 
realized before that you actually get some nutrition from a potion of 
booze. With my shinny new ring of slow digestion, I had nearly drank 
myself to death. So I took it off and worked on some other alchemy while 
I waited to burn off some of the booze. I alchemized up enough potions 
of full healing to increase my HP from 246 to 733 and still have enough 
for my ascension run. I also did well on potions of gain level and was 
able to stash 25 cursed potions of gain level in Gehennom and had 
several more to carry in my BoH. I finally got unsatiated, and finished 
off my booze. I got another wish and decided, with the malignant auras 
of the ascension run looming ahead, to try for Magicbane. I got really 
lucky and got the blessed rustproof +2 Magicbane at turn 110,312.

I spent a few hundred more turns packing up stuff to take to Gehennom 
and to the planes, fine tuning my armor enchantment, and refreshing all 
my spells. I left for Gehennom at turn 110,967 and stopped in the VotD 
only long enough to read another cursed scroll of teleportation. Three 
soldiers from the castle teleported with me to the next lower level. 
They were no problem. I used spells of magic mapping and detect treasure 
on each level of Gehennom and then dug a path between the two stairways. 
In my previous game, I had also dug out the outer ring of the level to 
make it easier on levels where the mysterious force intervened. That had 
work pretty well for me, so I did it this time as well. That also helped 
give me enough time to regenerate my mana for the spells. I stashed 10 
cursed potions of gain level by the upstairs of level 29, protected them 
with Elbereth and covered them with a boulder. And some people call me 
paranoid.

Asmodeus' Lair was on level 32. I dug down to the next level, which 
turned out to be Juiblex's Swamp. I found the upstairs,
engraved Elbereth with Magicbane, and climbed up. Asmo and I exchanged 
blows a couple of times and he zipped off to the upstairs to heal. I 
moved to the downstairs and went down as soon as he returned. He 
followed me down and I stood on the stairs (with the Elbereth engraving) 
and proceeded to slice and dice him with my silver saber. He croaked at 
turn 112,129. Juiblex turned up and joined Asmo wherever dead demons go, 
nine turns later. While crossing Juiblex's Swamp, I noticed a green 
slime. I decided to go ahead and genocide them as a preemptive strike. I 
looked in my Goodies bag for a scroll of genocide, but had forgot to 
bring any. So I made a quick detour back to base camp to get some. While 
there, I decided to eliminate N's and R's as well. N's because a Golden 
Naga had really pissed me off when I was working my way through the 
Castle by cursing some of my stuff and alerting everybody in the Castle 
to my presence. And R's just because I don't like them and I could do it.

I returned to level 34, again picking up three hitchhiking soldiers in 
the VotD. I dispatched them and mapped the level which turned out to be 
Balzebuub's Lair. Again I dug down, mapped the level, and dug my escape 
paths. A cockatrice showed up and left a corpse, so I paid Balzebuub a 
visit and whacked him with the rubber chicken at turn 112,391. I picked 
up a few treasures and returned to level 35. I finished clearing my 
escape paths and stashed 15 cursed potions of gain level by the down 
stairs, using the same precautions as on level 29. That should see me 
safely across the three no teleport levels with a margin of safety for 
the mysterious force. Orcus Town was on level 37 and again I dug down to 
the next level, bypassing Orcus for the time being. Level 38 had the 
stairs to Vlad's Tower, which was annoying because now I didn't know 
which up stairs led to Vlad and which, to Orcus. I cleared my escape 
paths, but no cockatrice was forthcoming so I proceeded on down.

Level 41 was the top level of Rodney's Tower. I always carry a few 
blessed scrolls of magic mapping with me, and when I find Rodney's level 
(via telepathy upon arriving on the level), I use a blessed scroll of 
magic mapping, rather than a spell, to reveal the location of the secret 
doors. I did this on the next two levels as well, so I know where all 
the (now not so) secret doors are when I come back. Level 41 was the 
Fake Wiz 1 level, which contained the portal to Rodney's complex. 
Normally, I go in and clear out the first two levels at this time, but I 
didn't now in order to minimize duplicated travel. Level 45 was the Fake 
Wiz 2 level and then level 47 had no down stairs. I found the vibrating 
square fairly quickly at turn 117,466, marked it with a big X made by 
dropping gold pieces and left the Bell of Opening there. I level 'ported 
back to level 38 to deal with with Vlad and Orcus. I dug a wide path 
between the 3 stairways while waiting for a cockatrice to spawn.

I finally grew impatient waiting for a cockatrice and wrote a cursed 
scroll of genocide. Neither of the first two I killed left a corpse. I 
was starting to worry a little. I checked my armor and I was wearing 
gauntlets of power to help me stay unburdened, so I switched back to my 
gauntlets of dexterity. I was a little uncomfortable taking off my 
gloves with cockatrices around, but it went OK, and the next one left a 
corpse. I don't know if that was a coincidence or not. I tucked the 
corpse in my bag, made my way to the closest up stairs, put on my ring 
of levitation, wielded the rubber chicken, and went up the stairs. Damn! 
Vlad's tower, wrong stairs. Undid it all and went back down stairs. I 
ran to the other stairs, dodging the remaining cockatrices using the 
nice wide path I had dug, and repeated the procedure. At turn 119,128, I 
turned Orcus into a statue. I made statues of several of the other 
denizens of Orcus Town and used my silver saber on the shades, 
skeletons, ghosts, and other less substantial inhabitants. I once found 
Grayswandir in one of the abandoned shops in Orcus Town, so I always 
check them out but didn't find anything noteworthy. I did kill my first 
black dragon and got my disintegration resistance at turn 119,681. I 
busted up the statue of Orcus and claimed my wand of death. Getting the 
wand at full power is one of the reasons I like to whack Orcus with the 
rubber chicken. So time for Vlad.

There was nothing noteworthy about the first two levels of Vlad's tower. 
But then, on the top level, something wonderful happened. Often (well, 
not all that often since I'd only ascended 5 times previously) I don't 
bother checking all those trunks in Vlad's tower since my Ascension Kit 
is pretty much complete by this time. Today, however, I decided to check 
them even though the time pressure is really mounting (it's late 
afternoon on 11/29 by now). And what do I find in the fourth chest on 
the top level: a wand of wishing(0:2)  at turn 120,269. I decided to 
have another go at the MKOT. I got the Castle wand out of my goodies bag 
and used its two remaining wishes with no luck. Then with the first wish 
from the new wand, I struck pay dirt and was blasted by the power of the 
Master Key of Thievery at turn 120,326. I took this as a very good omen 
and felt my ascension was now very much in the realm of possibility. As 
usual, Vlad was no problem; he fell easily to my silver saber. I felt 
out of place three times on his throne and then it vanished, but I was 
more than satisfied with my visit to Vlad's tower. I picked up the 
candelabrum at turn 120,374. 

I couldn't remember if I could level 'port out of Vlad's Tower or not, 
but it was a fairly short hike back to level 38 and once there, I level 
'ported to level 44 and traversed the portal to level 43 at turn 
120,507. I worked my way through Rodney's tower complex without major 
incident. I zapped Rodney with a wand of death and picked up the Book of 
the Dead at turn 121,014. A quick level 'port to the VS level, a short 
hike to the VS itself, and I performed the invocation at turn 121,076. I 
had been playing more or less straight for about 18 hours at this point, 
so I decided to take a break for a few hours and hopefully grab at least 
a short nap.

I took a break for about 5 hours, but was too keyed up to get a proper 
nap. I dozed for a bit a couple of times, but don't think I ever got 
properly asleep. OK, when I left off, I had just performed the 
invocation, so I went downstairs and entered the Sanctum. Due to weight 
problems, I decided to dump the Invocation items. Although I had learned 
most spells, I never found a spellbook of charm monster. So I decided to 
use another wish and wished for one now. I planned to use it here in the 
Sanctum and on the Planes to make some meat shields and maybe even a 
useful pet. But an earlier suboptimal decision interfered with that 
plan. I wanted to swap out my amulet of reflection for one of life 
saving as an added extra level of insurance against YASD. That meant I 
needed another source of reflection. Since rangers can't two weapon, I 
decided to go with a shield of reflection. But shields of reflection 
really kill your spell casting ability, so I had to take it off every 
time I wanted to cast a spell. And I kept forgetting to put it back on. 
I learned the charm monster spell and dumped the book for weight 
considerations. Besides, I wasn't expecting the game to last for another 
20K turns.

I switched weapons to the silver saber for the graveyard and promptly 
got a malignant aura cursing my ring of free action. I made it the rest 
of the way through the graveyard without much trouble. I switch back to 
Magicbane. At the end of the corridor between the graveyard and the main 
room, one of the priests started summoning insects. I took off my shield 
to make meat shields of the insects and forgot to rewield it after the 
spell. A few turns later, a priest blew up my rings of conflict and slow 
digestion with a lightning bolt and I didn't have backups for either 
one. I fought on and made my to the main room. I used wands of light and 
secret door detection to find the temple door. I went in and dealt with 
the nasties the priest summoned and finally managed to kill him. I 
hadn't found a suitable pet to do my dirty work for me. As usual, 
Moloch's lightning bolts were a joke since I remembered to keep my 
shield on. I picked up the Amulet of Yendor at turn 121,326, verified 
its authenticity by attempting to bag it, named it "The Real McCoy" and 
rose up through the ceiling on the next turn.

The run back to base camp was exceptionally easy. Rodney only showed up 
once and got promptly zapped by a wand of death. The mysterious force 
struck only ONCE! And that was only to the same level, so I would have 
had to cross level 32, Asmodeus's Lair a second time, but I just used 
another of my c !ofGL. I picked up my stashes of GL potions and zipped 
through the Lairs of the Demon Princes (or whatever the hell they are), 
the VotD, the Castle, and Medusa's level pretty much without 
confrontation. I arrived back at base camp at about turn 121,987 and had 
enough c !ofGL left to take me all the way to level 1. Because of the 
ring problem in the Sanctum, I had to poly up some replacements (and 
back ups, this time). I decided to throw some potions and scrolls into 
the poly pile as well and got enough scrolls of charging to boost my 
Power from 136 to 530 with a nice reserve for my wands of death. Used up 
the stray healing potions I had picked up and boosted HP from 733 to 
772, again with a nice reserve. I hadn't packed as carefully as I should 
have and was having trouble getting unburdened, making allowances for 
the stuff I would jettison on the plane of earth, remaining wands of 
digging and pick-axe. Hostiles seemed to be spawning at a faster than 
usual pace and I kept getting interrupted to deal with them. I don't 
know if that is a consequence of having the Amulet, or if it was just my 
imagination. Finally, at turn 122,639, I left base camp for the final 
time.

I checked my gear on level 1 and seemed to have all the necessary items. 
I climbed the stairs at turn 122,693 on 11/30, the last day of the 
tournament. I zapped Rodney with a wand of death for the third and final 
time, killed off his flunkies, and used a confused scroll of gold 
detection to find the portal. I dug my way to the portal and dumped my 
pick-axe and wands of digging. I changed my speed boots for levitation 
boots, swapped the ring of slow digestion for one of conflict and 
stepped thru the portal to the Plane of Air. With the ring of conflict, 
it went a little smoother that the previous time, but I still got 
engulfed by air elementals too many times. The MKOT paid off here 
though, and I got through without taking serious damage. Found the 
portal via another confused ?ofGD and slowly worked my way there. Plane 
of Fire was relatively uneventful, found the portal, yadda yadda yadda. 
Plane of Water always seems slow, but it's not much of a hassle without 
the ;'s. I remembered to replace the ring of conflict with the ring of 
slow digestion before activating the portal, and then, at turn 123,043, 
I arrived on the Astral Plane. 

I changed back into my speed boots and surveyed the lay out. Famine was 
on the right; Death, in the center; and Pestilence, on the left. With 2 
wands of death and plenty of charging scrolls, I again elected to save 
Death for last. I landed to the right, so I decided to go to the right 
and face Famine first. Zap the wand of death and Famine falls. Climb 
over his carcass and zap the wand of teleport to clear a path. Dodge and 
weave my way to the door to the temple courtyard, unlock and open it, 
zap the wand of teleport to clear the way, work my way up to the temple 
door, unlock and open again, and force my way in. I make it to the altar 
and check it. Lo and behold, in another stoke of luck, it's an altar to 
Mars (Chaotic) and my main man. That's it! I'm standing on the brink of 
success. Gee, that was almost too easy. Maybe I should get out 
Strombringer and go level drain Famine until I can tame him for some 
extra style points.Ha! Not bloody likely! At turn 123,079, I offered the 
Amulet and ascended with my friendly Angel.

